# Versioning

This repo is at **SemVer**. The current release is whatever `__version__` says
in `src/edgekit/__init__.py` (pyproject reads it from there). Do not ship a
behavior change without bumping that string and adding a `CHANGELOG.md` entry.

## When you finish a change

1. Decide the bump (see below).
2. Set `__version__` in `src/edgekit/__init__.py`.
3. Add a `## [X.Y.Z] — YYYY-MM-DD` section at the top of `CHANGELOG.md` (below
   the intro) with one or two bullets on **why**.
4. Do not edit `version` in `pyproject.toml` — it is dynamic.

## What to bump

| Change | Bump | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Bug fix, copy, small hardening | PATCH `1.0.0` → `1.0.1` | installer TTY abort, diagnostics timeout |
| New command, user-visible feature | MINOR `1.0.0` → `1.1.0` | `edgekit update`, `firewall setup` |
| Breaking CLI/config/API change | MAJOR `1.0.0` → `2.0.0` | rename env vars, drop a command |

Docs-only, comments, tests-only, or formatting: **no bump**.

## Checks

`tests/test_version.py` fails if `__version__` is not SemVer or is missing from
`CHANGELOG.md`. Run that test after the bump.
